virglrenderer: Venus views and samplers within their image, buffer and enums

What: vkr checks a guest's views and samplers before the Mac's Vulkan driver
gets them:
- vkCreateImageView: a view type of the spec, a 3D view only of a 3D image, a
  format the driver has features for at the image's tiling and of the image's
  texel block size (multi-planar images: not checked), levels and layers inside
  the image (a 3D image's slices at the view's base level for other view types),
  6 layers for a cube and a multiple of 6 for a cube array.
- vkCreateBufferView: a buffer with texel usage and a format the driver has those
  texel buffer features for, an offset inside the buffer and aligned (to
  minTexelBufferOffsetAlignment, or by the per-format rule when the guest turned
  texel buffer alignment on or uses Vulkan 1.3), whole texels inside the buffer, at
  most maxTexelBufferElements. vkr keeps each buffer's size and usage.
- vkCreateSampler: filters, mipmap mode, address modes, compare op and border
  colour are values of the spec.
The guest makes views and samplers without waiting for an answer, so a refused
one ends the app's Venus context at once, with the reason in QEMU's log (made
silently without the host object, the app's first use of it would end the
context anyway, without a reason; a clamped range would hide the app's bug).
Type pairs that live on both drivers are not refused (a cube view without
CUBE_COMPATIBLE, a 2D view of a 3D image without 2D_ARRAY_COMPATIBLE, a 1D view
of a 2D image). Uses vkr_context_refuse and vkr_format_table.h from
virgl-venus-image-limits.patch; can be dropped on its own.
Why: KosmicKrisp makes Metal texture views and texel buffer textures of the
guest's values, and Metal ends the process on a level or slice past the texture,
a cube view of 5 layers, a 3D view of a 2D texture, another texel size, a texel
buffer wider than 2^28 texels; KosmicKrisp crashes on a format it has no entry for
and ends on sampler magFilter 7 (M4, macOS 27, one process per case, 3 runs).
A texel view past its buffer lives on both drivers, but the GPU would then read and
write outside the buffer (a GPU fault resets the GPU).
Upstream: OmacVM policy, as virgl-venus-image-limits.patch (ADR 0065).
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-image-limits.c (build time): the view, texel view and
sampler cases end the child before the patch and end only the context after it;
views and texel views in range, a cube of 6, an sRGB view of a mutable image and a
BC1 block view still work.

